MedQA (data/icdm2026/medqa_answers.csv)
Only case index numbers (case_id of the form medqa-<index>) and answer letters are shipped. No question text, options or explanations. The index is the row position in the 1,273-question MedQA-USMLE four-option test split. The license of the Hugging Face release (bigbio/med_qa) is listed as unknown. See the original source for terms. Source: Jin et al., "What Disease Does This Patient Have? A Large-Scale Open Domain Question Answering Dataset from Medical Exams," Applied Sciences, 2021.

MedMCQA (data/icdm2026/medmcqa_answers.csv)
Only case index numbers (case_id of the form medmcqa-<index>) and answer letters are shipped. No question text and no original identifiers. The index is the row position in the MedMCQA validation split as loaded for the ICDM study (2,816 single-answer questions of 4,183). The dataset metadata (openlifescienceai/medmcqa) lists Apache 2.0. See the original source for terms. Source: Pal et al., "MedMCQA: A Large-scale Multi-Subject Multi-Choice Dataset for Medical domain Question Answering," Conference on Health, Inference, and Learning (CHIL), 2022.

Model outputs (both ICDM files)
Each output is a single answer letter. Models: Llama 3 8B Instruct Lite (Meta), Qwen 2.5 7B Instruct Turbo (Alibaba), Gemma 3n E4B it (Google), DeepSeek-V3 (DeepSeek), GPT-4o (OpenAI), Flan-T5-base (Google, used as a near-random control). Outputs were collected in April to May 2026 through Together.ai and the OpenAI API. Use of each model is subject to its developer's and provider's terms. See the original sources.

HELM Lite outputs (outside/data/helm_lite_medqa_answers.csv)
Answer letters, reference letters and instance ids extracted from public per-instance outputs of Stanford CRFM's HELM Lite benchmark, release v1.13.0, MedQA scenario (bucket crfm-helm-public). No question text is shipped. The models were run by HELM, not by the author of this package. Source URLs and SHA-256 hashes are in outside/SOURCES.tsv. No license for the per-instance outputs in the crfm-helm-public bucket was found stated at the source when read on 2026-11-12. This file is not relicensed under CC BY 4.0, and the model developers' terms apply. MedQA terms above also apply. Reference: P. Liang et al., "Holistic Evaluation of Language Models," Transactions on Machine Learning Research, 2023.

SGOF cohort (data/sgof2026/)
Source cohort: Fuh S-C, Fiori LM, Turecki G, Nagy C, Li Y. "Multi-omic modeling of antidepressant response implicates dynamic immune and inflammatory changes in individuals who respond to treatment." PLOS ONE 18(5): e0285123 (2023), https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0285123, licensed CC BY 4.0. The labels come from Patient_condition.csv in the article's Supporting information (S1 File). Changes: binary responder labels re-keyed to anonymous ids; all other files are model outputs derived by the author. No genotype, gene expression or DNA methylation values are redistributed. The ids p000 to p110 are the row order of the processed matrix used in the SGOF study and are not participant ids from the source.
